---
title: Title
description: Headings with optional introductions, subtitles and borders.
show_title: true
show_description: true
hide_table_of_contents: true
show_source: true
---

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-4">Default styles</h2>
<p class="mx-3">These examples use the component defaults, with and without a bottom border.</p>

<twig:block-title
    class="container my-4"
    title="Make room for your next idea"
    subtitle="Bring your team and your tools together. Explore the <a href='#title-options'>available options</a> to find what works for you."
/>

<twig:block-title
    class="container my-4"
    title="A clear starting point"
    subtitle="Use a border when the heading needs a visible separation from the following content."
    :border="true"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5" id="title-options">Optional introduction</h2>
<p class="mx-3">The introduction appears above the heading. It uses plain text and follows the requested alignment.</p>

<twig:block-title
    class="container my-4"
    eyebrow="Project overview"
    title="Turn your ideas into a shared plan"
    subtitle="An introduction, a heading and a subtitle form one component."
/>

<twig:block-title
    class="container my-4"
    align="left"
    eyebrow="Getting started"
    title="Keep the next step in focus"
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">An addressable heading</h2>
<p class="mx-3"><code>id</code> identifies the component root. <code>headingId</code> identifies the heading itself, so a section can refer to it through <code>aria-labelledby</code>.</p>

<twig:block-title
    id="title-accessible"
    headingId="title-accessible-heading"
    class="container my-4"
    role="region"
    aria-labelledby="title-accessible-heading"
    :level="3"
    align="start"
    eyebrow="Explore the details"
    title="A heading with its own identifier"
    subtitle="This named region refers to the heading while the component keeps its independent root identifier."
/>

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Heading levels</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Choose the heading level for the document structure. The component styling stays consistent.</p>
{% for level in [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6] %}
    <twig:block-title
        class="container my-4"
        :level="level"
        align="start"
        title="Heading level {{ level }}"
    />
{% endfor %}

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Long content and alignment</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Compare start, center and end alignment with long content on narrow screens. The aliases left and right are also supported.</p>
{% for align in ['start', 'center', 'end'] %}
    <twig:block-title
        class="container my-4"
        align="{{ align }}"
        :border="true"
        eyebrow="Resources for planning, collaboration and everyday work"
        title="A longer heading introducing the complete configuration and synchronization guide"
        subtitle="A subtitle with more context and a <a href='#title-options'>link to the instructions</a>, so wrapping and alignment can be compared on a small screen."
    />
{% endfor %}

<h2 class="h4 mx-3 mt-5">Optional CSS variable overrides</h2>
<p class="mx-3">Only this example changes two variables: a fluid heading size and a narrower reading width. The examples above use the default styles.</p>

<twig:block-title
    class="container my-4"
    style="--title-font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 2.5rem); --title-max-width: 22ch;"
    align="right"
    eyebrow="A focused introduction"
    title="Adjust the size and reading width for your content"
    subtitle="The component accepts a fluid size while its other styles keep their default values."
/>
